  "claim_boundary": "This is a post hoc equivalence reading of already-computed intervals, not a confirmatory or preregistered test, and it re-runs no resampling. Passing a margin bounds the size of any residual-rule advantage on the evaluated ligand-target pairs of these three benchmarks; it does not show the two rules are identical, does not extend to other chemical supports, target panels, scoring functions or endpoints, and does not license the word 'prespecified' anywhere. The conservative union widens the interval and therefore makes every decision here harder, not easier. The equivalence holds on the primary strata only: the exploratory binder-only strata (DAVIS both_uncensored, PKIS2 both_active) show intervals excluding zero in favour of the residual rule and fail every margin on this grid, so no global 'the rules are equivalent' statement is supported.",
